{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'git diff --stat && git diff -- src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc && cat collab/yang-clojure/1795017757000-architect-cc4-dart-map-order-ruling.gpt-6-astra.findings.md'","aggregated_output":" src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc                         | 57 +++++++++++--\n src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc                   | 13 ++-\n src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj                           |  7 +-\n .../yang/clojure/cc4-replay-snapshots.edn          | 23 +++--\n test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc               | 97 ++++++++++++++++++++--\n 5 files changed, 169 insertions(+), 28 deletions(-)\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc b/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\nindex d2094a97..47af7fee 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\n@@ -299,6 +299,16 @@\n      :else false)))\n \n \n+(defn- content-root\n+  \"The canonical semantic-bytecode root of one compiled child: the content\n+   address of its projected executable content. Constructed collections\n+   order their operands by these addresses (constructed-collections-v1);\n+   the projection here is temporary compile-time data, never a published\n+   root or ordering table.\"\n+  [ast]\n+  (:root (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)))\n+\n+\n (defn- compile-constructed-collection\n   \"Lower a collection literal with dynamic elements to constructor calls over\n    existing portable primitives, so unquoted vectors/maps/sets evaluate their\n@@ -306,20 +316,55 @@\n \n    [e1 e2 ...]  => (conj [] e1 e2 ...)\n    #{e1 e2 ...} => (conj #{} e1 e2 ...)\n-   {k1 v1 ...}  => (assoc {} k1 v1 k2 v2 ...)\"\n+   {k1 v1 ...}  => (assoc {} k1 v1 k2 v2 ...)\n+\n+   A host map or set has no portable iteration order, so a map's pairs and\n+   a set's elements enter the operand vector in compiled-content order\n+   (constructed-collections-v1): each child compiles once, pairs sort\n+   ascending by jing/canonical-compare over the two-element vector\n+   [key-root value-root] of the children's projected roots (key-root\n+   primary, value-root secondary), set elements by their own root, after\n+   the unchanged seed operand and before the unchanged operator resolution\n+   and tail mark. Equal sort keys are equal executable content under the\n+   content-address integrity contract, so a tie keeps its occurrences and\n+   needs no further tie-break; no child is recompiled, deduplicated or\n+   evaluated, and each compiled AST keeps its own attached metadata. A\n+   vector retains its written element order.\"\n   [form tail? env macro-env]\n   (let [ctor (cond\n                (vector? form) ['conj []]\n                (set? form) ['conj #{}]\n                :else ['assoc {}])\n         [op seed] ctor\n-        args (if (map? form)\n-               (into [] (interleave (keys form) (vals form)))\n-               (vec form))\n+        compile-child #(compile-form % false env macro-env)\n+        ;; each pair/element keeps its compiled ASTs and their content keys\n+        ;; together, so sorting never recompiles or loses an occurrence\n+        sorted-children\n+        (cond\n+          (vector? form) {:order :written, :children (mapv compile-child form)}\n+          (map? form)\n+          {:order :canonical\n+           :records (mapv (fn [k v]\n+                            (let [ck (compile-child k)\n+                                  cv (compile-child v)]\n+                              {:sort-key [(content-root ck) (content-root cv)]\n+                               :children [ck cv]}))\n+                          (keys form) (vals form))}\n+          :else\n+          {:order :canonical\n+           :records (mapv (fn [e]\n+                            (let [ce (compile-child e)]\n+                              {:sort-key [(content-root ce)]\n+                               :children [ce]}))\n+                          form)})\n+        operands (case (:order sorted-children)\n+                   :written (:children sorted-children)\n+                   (into [] (mapcat :children)\n+                         (sort-by :sort-key jing/canonical-compare\n+                                  (:records sorted-children))))\n         call {:type :application,\n               :operator {:type :variable, :name op},\n-              :operands (into [{:type :literal, :value seed}]\n-                              (map #(compile-form % false env macro-env) args))}]\n+              :operands (into [{:type :literal, :value seed}] operands)}]\n     (cond-> call tail? (assoc :tail? true))))\n \n \ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc b/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc\nindex 2668cb67..6a9d364b 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc\n@@ -45,11 +45,18 @@\n    occurrence carries `:yang/call-site` in the frontend-metadata side\n    table, finalized over the post-expansion tree that executes and\n    retained beside a published module's manifest — and that promise is\n-   a support claim, so the revision and the support profile name it;\n-   the shared legacy profiles no longer describe this frontend.\"\n+   a support claim, so the revision and the support profile name it.\n+   Revision c1-2 additionally declares the constructed-collections\n+   lowering profile: a dynamically constructed map or set literal now\n+   orders its constructor operands by compiled content\n+   (:yang.clojure/constructed-collections-v1), a one-time canonical\n+   shift for affected newly compiled artifacts; the C1 support claim,\n+   the C1 marker value and the execution grammar versions are\n+   unchanged.\"\n   []\n   (assoc (manifest :yang/clojure :clojure)\n-         :yang.frontend/revision \"c1-1\"\n+         :yang.frontend/revision \"c1-2\"\n+         :yang.frontend/lowering-profile :yang.clojure/constructed-collections-v1\n          :yang.frontend/support-profile :yang.clojure/c1))\n \n \ndiff --git a/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj b/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj\nindex d0b316de..4fbfe588 100644\n--- a/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj\n+++ b/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj\n@@ -347,7 +347,10 @@\n    \"yin.vm.ucf.fencing-rows-test\" \"yin.vm.ucf.holder.reader-test\"\n    \"yin.vm.ucf.holder.writer-test\" \"yin.vm.ucf.holder.driver-test\"\n    ;; cc4: the frontend's own replay-equality gate is mandatory on Jolt.\n-   \"yang.clojure-callsite-test\"])\n+   \"yang.clojure-callsite-test\"\n+   ;; constructed-collections-v1 (fix round, ruling 1795017757000): the\n+   ;; canonical operand-ordering battery.\n+   \"yang.clojure-collection-order-test\"])\n \n \n ;; Read only namespace tokens, never evaluate forms or resolve reader branches.\n@@ -358,7 +361,7 @@\n   [test-root included-nses excluded-suites]\n   (let [dirs [\"dao/host\" \"dao/jing\" \"dao/data\" \"dao/space\" \"dao/stream\" \"yin/vm\" \"yin/repl\"]\n         bare [\"dao/jing_test\" \"dao/stream_test\" \"dao/data_test\" \"yin/vm_test\" \"yin/repl_test\"\n-              \"yang/clojure_callsite_test\"]\n+              \"yang/clojure_callsite_test\" \"yang/clojure_collection_order_test\"]\n         extensions [\"clj\" \"cljc\" \"cljs\" \"cljd\"]\n         files (->> (concat\n                      (mapcat #(->> (fs/glob (fs/path test-root %) \"**\")\ndiff --git a/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc b/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc\nindex b4ae083f..f27c7847 100644\n--- a/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc\n+++ b/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc\n@@ -952,6 +952,28 @@\n       (published :clj clj-result clj-spec)])))\n \n \n+(defn- collection-constructors\n+  \"The constructed-collection applications of compiled `ast`: an assoc over\n+   the {} seed or a conj over the []/#{} seed -- the yang.clojure\n+   collection emitter's output.\"\n+  [ast]\n+  (let [acc (atom [])]\n+    (walk/postwalk\n+      (fn [n]\n+        (when (and (map? n)\n+                   (= :application (:type