\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Completed-GMT: 2026-11-18 19:20:14 GMT\\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-19 02:20:14 +07:00\\n\\n**fix/constructed-collection-order r1 — implemented, all gates green on JVM/Node/Dart; Jolt honestly blocked by the inherited J2 manifest refusal. Nothing committed.**\\n\\n## The fix (inside the ruling's bounds table only)\\n\\n- **`src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc`** — `compile-constructed-collection` now compiles each map key/value (set element) once, takes each compiled child's root via the existing `vm/ast->semantic-bytecode` projection (new private `content-root`), and sorts pairs ascending by `jing/canonical-compare` over `[key-root value-root]` (set elements by their root; vectors untouched), after the unchanged seed, with operator/tail/metadata semantics unchanged. The reproduced arity map now emits `fn, reason, argc` on every host — the ruling's pinned order (key roots `1e0366…`/`81b62c…`/`8930bf…`).\\n- **`src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc`** — manifest `c1-1 → c1-2`, lowering profile `:yang.clojure/constructed-collections-v1`; C1 claim/marker/SPI/grammar unchanged.\\n- **Tests** — new portable `test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc` covering all seven required families (RED first: 10 tests / 91,387 assertions / 0 errors failing pre-fix, log archived), plus a focused constructor-order deftest and helper in `clojure_callsite_test.cljc`; the eight-member cohort preserved.\\n\\n## Gates (exact commands, counts, logs in the evidence dir)\\n\\n| Lane | Result |\\n|---|---|\\n| JVM callsite `clojure -M:test -n yang.clojure-callsite-test` | 46 tests / 605 assertions / 0 failures |\\n| JVM ordering (new ns) | 10 / 91,387 / 0 |\\n| JVM `clojure-test` + `frontend-test` + `frontend-catalog-test` | 116 / 1,082 / 0 |\\n| Node (shadow-cljs, both selectors) | 41/516 and 10/91,387, 0 failures — all eight snapshots match |\\n| Dart (`cljd_agg`, both selectors) | 41 and 10 registered