 | 41 and 10 registered: **all passed** — the originally diverging host matches the JVM bundle |\\n| Jolt (`jolt_j2_lane core --only …`, both) | **exit 1 at manifest, 0 children** — refusal names the four inherited unlisted namespaces (`yin.repl.php-parser-test`, `yin.vm.code-entry-test`, `yin.vm.machine-data-test`, `yin.vm.provenance-test`); owner dependency recorded, no exclusions added, my namespace added to `included` + bare inventory only |\\n| kondo on touched files | 0 errors, 1 pre-existing `yin.repl.query` warning; `git diff --check` clean |\\n\\n## Re-pin\\n\\nOnly `:argument-vector` and `:lower-unit` changed canonical bytes (the defect site); six members byte-identical. Pre-fix bundle archived verbatim (`cc4-replay-snapshots-prefix-c1-1.edn`, sha `5f28913f…` matches r2's pin); post-fix bundle re-recorded for the complete cohort; ledger with every digest transition under `collab/yang-clojure/1795028800000-fixorder-evidence/constructed-collections-repin-ledger-v1.md`. Legacy artifact retained (`constructed-collections-legacy-c1-1.cbor`): it loads and still executes to its old `{0 :b}` while fresh c1-2 compiles yield `{0 :a}`.\\n\\n## Boundaries reported (not worked around)\\n\\n- Whole-**element** ties for sets are unconstructable at the form API (every host set constructor collapses two NaNs); recorded in the test. Map ties/secondary-key cases are reached via NaN keys built with `assoc` (literals reject NaN duplicates under Java `equals`); metadata-variant equal keys collapse silently under host `=`.\\n- ClojureDart has no `array-map` — portable `insertion-map` builder, documented.\\n- No dependency outside the bounds table other than the J2 refusal; r2's divergence evidence untouched.\\n\\nDeliverable: `collab/yang-clojure/1795028788000-engineer-fix-constructed-collection-order-r1.glm-5.3.findings.md` (worktree copy) with SHA-256 pins, commands, counts, and the ledger; temporary driver/scratch namespaces deleted.\",\"ttft_ms\":7837,\"type\":\"result\",\"d