script|dart|cpp]\n                                 ; or: bb gen:antlr\n\n   1. Read the vendored grammars (antlr/<grammar>/*.g4, MIT, committed) and\n      fetch the remaining pinned files at the manifest's revision (cached\n      under build/, re-fetched only when absent); refuse any digest mismatch.\n   2. For each manifest :targets entry (:java, :javascript, :dart), stage the\n      grammars and that target's helpers, applying the recorded patches (the\n      Java helpers also get their package clause prepended).\n   3. Run the pinned ANTLR tool with the target's flags, then apply the\n      target's recorded :output-patches to the files it wrote.\n   4. Java only: compile with the host javac into build/antlr/<g>/classes,\n      which deps.edn puts on the classpath.\n   5. Digest every generated source file of the target and compare with the\n      target's recorded :generated digests; a mismatch fails the build.\n\n   `clj -M:antlr-gen discover` prints the head commit of the grammar path, for\n   deliberately moving the pin. Nothing here runs at admission time.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.edn :as edn]\n    [clojure.java.io :as io]\n    [clojure.pprint :as pprint]\n    [clojure.string :as str])\n  (:import\n    (io.github.rctcwyvrn.blake3\n      Blake3)\n    (java.net\n      URI)\n    (java.net.http\n      HttpClient\n      HttpClient$Redirect\n      HttpRequest\n      HttpResponse$BodyHandlers)\n    (javax.tools\n      ToolProvider)))\n\n\n(def ^:dynamic *grammar* \"python3\")\n\n\n(defn- manifest-path\n10:      under build/, re-fetched only when absent); refuse any digest mismatch.\n16:   4. Java only: compile with the host javac into build/antlr/<g>/classes,\n19:      target's recorded :generated digests; a mismatch fails the build.\n59:    (.hexdigest b)))\n106:  \"Each pinned file, vendored or fetched, digest-checked. A vendored file\n127:        (throw (ex-info \"Grammar digest or ASCII check failed\"\n157:  \"The source extensions a target keeps and digests: its :exts when given\n223:(defn- generated-digests\n240:(defn- compile-java!\n258:        (throw (ex-info \"javac failed\" {:exit rc}))))\n266:        digests (generated-digests out (target-exts target))\n268:    (spit (io/file out \"generated-digests.edn\")\n269:          (with-out-str (pprint/pprint digests)))\n274:      (when-not (= expected digests)\n275:        (throw (ex-info \"Generated sources differ from the recorded digests\"\n276:                        {:target tname, :expected expected, :actual digests}))))\n277:    (when (= :java tname) (compile-java! out))\n278:    (println \"generated\" (count digests) (name tname) \"files in\" (.getPath out))\n280:      (println \"no :generated digests recorded yet for\" tname \"; record these:\")\n281:      (pprint/pprint digests))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
